  "interpretation": [
    "S red/tag1 bias is overwhelmingly in the learned content-scoring MLP: the within-parent tag1-minus-tag0 mean is +4.9284056 learned logits plus -0.00105345 fixed-novelty logits, yielding +4.9273521 total. Learned logit differences are positive and larger in absolute value than fixed differences in all 1152 S parents.",
    "The fixed novelty term remains part of the scoring rule and can favor salient items in R/D (mean contrasts roughly +0.46/+0.47), but it is not the main source of this S tag-color preference. Its S aggregate contribution is approximately -0.02% of the total mean logit gap.",
    "These are additive logit decompositions. A fraction of a logit gap is not an attribution fraction for nonlinear softmax probability, reader MSE, or causality.",
    "The result locates an observed bias in the trained score network; it does not establish that softmax as a general aggregation architecture necessarily prefers red/tag1, or that this bias alone causes all reading failures.",
    "R/D within-parent salient-versus-normal contrasts compare items with potentially different roles. They quantify scores in the observed parents and should not be interpreted as isolated effects of rendering a cue salient."
  ],
